$ grove-backup --help (exit 0)
grove-backup — back up this grove's units to its bucket, then write the status

usage:
  grove-backup            one pass, as camper (the timer runs it every 3 hours)
  grove-backup --line     the one status line every surface prints
  grove-backup --adopt    as camper: this box writes the prefix its name already holds
  grove-backup --help     this text

a pass by hand, from ground: sudo systemctl start grove-backup.service

$ grove-backup --bogus (exit 2)
✋ ConstraintError: unknown argument '--bogus'
   └─ see: grove-backup --help

$ grove-backup --line extra (exit 2)
✋ ConstraintError: --line takes no other word
   └─ see: grove-backup --help

$ grove-backup --line (exit 0)
✓ <age> ago · 2 put · 5 skipped

$ grove-backup --adopt (exit 0)
✓ grove backup · this box now writes its name's prefix; the next pass lands

$ sudo grove-backup (exit 2)
✋ ConstraintError: grove-backup runs as camper, never as root
   └─ a pass by hand, from ground: sudo systemctl start grove-backup.service
